    <item>
      <title>Denle Chayote</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/projects/video/denle-chayote/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 15 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/projects/video/denle-chayote/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;vimeo-responsive &#34; style=&#34;margin: 2rem 0;&#34;&gt;
  &lt;iframe src=&#34;https://player.vimeo.com/video/910960727?responsive=1&#34;
          frameborder=&#34;0&#34;
          allow=&#34;autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture&#34;
          allowfullscreen&gt;
  &lt;/iframe&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;style&gt;
.vimeo-responsive {
  position: relative;
  padding-bottom: 56.25%;
  height: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
  max-width: 1067px;
  margin: 2rem auto;
}

.vimeo-responsive iframe {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
}

.vimeo-responsive.portrait {
  padding-bottom: 177.78%;
  max-width: 450px;
  margin: 2rem auto;
}

.vimeo-responsive.square {
  padding-bottom: 100%;
  max-width: 600px;
  margin: 2rem auto;
}

@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .vimeo-responsive.portrait,
  .vimeo-responsive.square {
    max-width: 90%;
  }
}
&lt;/style&gt;

This work is an attempt to delve into the complexities of identity, culture, and human connection while drawing inspiration from the narrative styles of TV and YouTube shows. Through the humanised character of a chayote, I explore themes of post-colonialism and cultural exchange, primarily inspired by my experiences in Oaxaca, Mexico. With a blend of humour and introspection, the viewer is invited to join me on a personal journey of exchange, fostering a deeper understanding of the shared human experience.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>that&#39;s you in the spotlight</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/projects/neither/spotlight/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 25 Mar 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/projects/neither/spotlight/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;div style=&#34;position: fixed; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; z-index: -1; overflow: hidden;&#34;&gt;
  &lt;img src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/backgrounds/spotlight-bg.jpeg&#34; style=&#34;width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: center top;&#34;&gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;project-bg-overlay&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;style&gt;
.project-bg-overlay {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5);
}

.dark .project-bg-overlay {
  background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);
}
&lt;/style&gt;

This work plays with the precarious nature of being seen (or even consumed) by the media we consume. It further layers an aspect of an alt-Hindu guru/diva figure whose virtual presence provides the audience with flimsy guidance and support as they find their image absorbed by the work. While you reminisce the inherent nostalgia of R.E.M’s Losing My Religion, she will help you either find or lose your faith.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
